# hryk

**English** · [简体中文](README.md)

`hryk` is the **equivalent short name** of [`haruyuki`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/haruyuki).

This package ships **no code of its own** — it is a thin forwarding manifest that depends on the
main package, so **installing it is the same as installing `haruyuki` itself**. Both command names
run the exact same program.

## Install

```bash
npm install -g hryk      # short name
npm install -g haruyuki  # long name
```

Either one gives you **both** commands: `hryk` and `haruyuki`.

## Usage

Whichever name you type, the behaviour is identical — **the long name is what appears in
user-facing text**.

```bash
hryk --version           # {{VERSION}} (Haruyuki)
haruyuki --version       # {{VERSION}} (Haruyuki)

hryk --new               # create a new conversation
haruyuki --agent <id>    # open a specific agent
```

## Version

This package's version `{{VERSION}}` is **locked exactly** to `{{MAIN}}@{{VERSION}}`, so the short
name can never pull a mismatched build of the main package. Both packages are always released with
the same version number.

## Update

```bash
npm install -g hryk@latest
```

## Documentation and data

Documentation, configuration and data all live with the main package:

- Usage and configuration: see [the `haruyuki` README](https://www.npmjs.com/package/haruyuki)
- Local data directory: `~/.haruyuki` (shared by both command names)

